      "content": "But that's what the officials say. I've seen plenty of people pointing out legitimate loopholes, like how easy it is to intercept ballots in mailboxes or how signature verification isn't always consistent. If there are actually flaws in the system, shouldn't that be treated as a serious threat to the election rather than just \"minor issues\"? It feels like you're brushing off the actual concerns people have.",
